Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.1 title screen fills 16:9 (backdrop mirrored into the gutters)

The title screen (PRESS START, New Game / Options / Load Game) ran with
gutter 0, a 4:3 picture pillarboxed on a 16:9 screen. Its backdrop is three
320x240 sheets plus eight animated sprites, with no art past the 4:3 edges.
With widescreen on, every backdrop sheet and animation frame is drawn twice
more, mirrored (scale -1) about x 0 and about x 320, so each gutter shows the
outer 53 columns reversed, meeting the picture at its edge; the edge fade's
triangles (an option is chosen) reach the picture's edges. The backdrop
calls dw3_port_widescreen_title_backdrop() every frame it is drawn: the
title overlay (STDWTITL also plays the movies and the still screen) gets the
menu gutter only while it is. Logo, menu and options stay in the middle 4:3
(native overlays, re-centred by the hosts). Off, nothing changes.

--- a/src/menus/title/background.c
+++ b/src/menus/title/background.c
@@ -1,6 +1,29 @@
 /* The title screen's background, and its eight looping sprite animations */
 
 #include "menus/title.h"
+#if PORT_HOST
+#include "port_widescreen.h"
+
+/* Widescreen (patch 0085): the backdrop has no art past the 4:3 edges, so
+   with a gutter each sheet is drawn twice more, mirrored about x 0 and about
+   x 320; the gutters show the outer columns reversed, meeting the picture at
+   its edges */
+static void STDWTITL_drawWide(SpriteDrawer *sprite, s32 *sheet, s32 frame, s32 x, s32 y) {
+    sprite->draw(sheet, frame, x, y);
+    if (dw3_port_widescreen_px() > 0) {
+        sprite->setScale(-ONE, ONE, ONE);
+        sprite->setPivot(0, 0);
+        sprite->draw(sheet, frame, x, y);
+        sprite->setPivot(SCREEN_WIDTH, 0);
+        sprite->draw(sheet, frame, x, y);
+        sprite->setScale(ONE, ONE, ONE);
+        sprite->setPivot(0, 0);
+    }
+}
+#define STDWTITL_DRAW(sprite, sheet, frame, x, y) STDWTITL_drawWide(&(sprite), (sheet), (frame), (x), (y))
